and [the booking-v3 hint issue](https://github.com/FrankiewiczMikolaj/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## Shared parser

The shared parser reads month-first while these tenants write dates day-first.
For example, R-41200 from harbour.dental reports a reminder for 7 April arriving for
4 July. The tenant directory identifies its locale as en-GB.

The exported classifier assigns day-first tenant reports here except form-channel
reports using booking-v3. Use the tenant's stored locale, not the reporter's browser
locale or intake tag. Fix and test parsing separately from the displayed form hint.

## Booking-v3 date hint

Booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but its form reads the date using the tenant's
convention. For day-first tenants, following that hint can swap the intended date.
R-41230 from copper.studio reports 1 June instead of 6 January; the tenant uses
es-ES and booking-v3, and the report channel is form.

This group is limited to form-channel reports for day-first booking-v3 tenants.
Their app and email reports stay in the parser group. Align the hint with the
accepted input and test both together; a parser fix alone does not demonstrate this
mismatch is resolved.

## Keep uncertain reports visible

The desk notes flag R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 as unusual timing or
one-day moves. The exported classifier assigns them to parser, but their wording does
not independently establish that cause. Keep their IDs counted exactly once and
investigate them; do not turn a possible timezone explanation into a confirmed bug.

## Triage and follow-up

The [written triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) and
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merge on normalized
subject alone. The interactive example instead compares causes. This disagreement
explains why the written policy is not enough to establish that every merged report
shares a fix.

Proposed practice: compare the report body and the tenant's locale, form and channel
before merging. Matching subjects are a search aid, not proof of a shared cause.
This is a recommendation, not an approved policy change. Leave accepted decision
0001 unchanged; any replacement needs a new decision record.

The grouping evidence retains source hashes and per-report assignments for audit.
The new download did not establish whether the desk has received additional reports
outside this export. The counts above apply only to the supplied snapshot.

